2. `map` entries definition: spec says "an entry function is one that is exported and called from outside the paths given." Code computes `called` by scanning all files outside `inside` for calls resolving to declarations inside `inside`. But `resolvedDeclaration` may return a declaration whose location is the definition; then it checks path inside. Then filters exported. But it uses `keyOf(located(...))` to match insideDefinitions which are keyed by definition.node location. For a function declaration, nodeOf location == declaration location, fine. But for arrow/effect-fn held in variable declarations, definitionsIn pushes the VariableDeclaration node, while `resolvedDeclaration` returns the VariableDeclaration too (valueDeclaration of the const symbol). Should match.

